# Keep the build context small and reproducible.
#
# A smaller context is not just faster: anything copied into the image is a place
# a stray .env or a developer's local secret file could end up baked into a layer
# where it is readable forever.

# Build artifacts: always regenerated, never a source of truth.
bin/
tmp/
*.test
*.out
coverage.*

# Local configuration. .env holds real credentials locally and must never enter an
# image layer.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Version control and editor noise: not needed by `go build`, and .git can be
# surprisingly large.
.git
.gitignore
.github
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store

# Documentation and CI files do not affect the binaries.
*.md
Makefile
